    <!-- Locke's mark: three vertical bars, square-edged to match the app's brutalist
         shape language (LockeShapes uses 0dp corners everywhere). Kept within the
         adaptive-icon safe zone (the centered ~66dp circle). Stepped ascending heights
         read as a rising streak/bar-chart rather than three identical ticks, and the
         tallest bar picks up the accent's dark-theme secondary tone as a quiet signal
         color -- the same role MossSecondary80 plays as `secondary` in the in-app
         Moss dark scheme (see Theme.kt), kept as a literal hex here since the launcher
         icon doesn't follow the user's selected in-app theme. -->
